## Comments

### Prefer self-explanatory code; comment **why**

```python
# ❌ Bad — narrates what the code obviously does
# Increment i by 1
i += 1

# ✅ Good — business or data quirk
# Source sends duplicate events within 60s; we keep the latest by ingest timestamp.
df = df.sort_values("ingested_at").drop_duplicates(subset=["event_id"], keep="last")
```

```sql
-- ✅ Good — source system quirk or SCD logic
-- HubSpot exports NULL deal_id for legacy rows; we map to -1 for the surrogate key table.
COALESCE(deal_id, -1) AS deal_surrogate_input
```

